\section*{SLE interfaces for weakly interacting planar Ising models}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a mathematical result relevant to this question in the selected manuscript. Weak finite-range perturbations of Ising contour energy are claimed to give chordal $\mathrm{SLE}_3$ interfaces at one domain-independent critical temperature, including signed perturbations.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} Fix $J>0$ and a signed finite-range potential $U$ on finite dual-edge sets, with $U(\varnothing)=0$ and square-lattice translation, rotation and reflection invariance. In a finite square-lattice spin domain $\Omega$ whose union of unit cells is the closure of a Jordan domain, choose two dual boundary marks and exterior stubs. Let $E_\Omega$ be dual edges crossing bonds with an endpoint in $\Omega$. Interior contours $P\subset E_\Omega$ have odd degrees at precisely the two marks; a finite exterior completion $P_o$ contains the stubs and has the same odd-degree marks. Sample contours with probability proportional to
\[
 \exp\left[-2\beta J|P|-\beta\lambda
 \sum_{\varnothing\ne X\subseteq P}\sum_{Y\subseteq P_o}U(X\cup Y)\right].
\]
Thus interactions joining interior and exterior occupied edges remain present. Resolve a degree-four contour vertex by pairing north with east and south with west, obtaining the oriented chord $\gamma(P)$ between stub midpoints. There is $\lambda_0(J,U)>0$ and a domain-independent $\beta_c(J,U,\lambda)>0$, with $\beta_c(J,U,0)=\log(1+\sqrt2)/(2J)$, such that for $|\lambda|<\lambda_0$, deterministic marked approximations of any bounded Jordan $(D;a,b)$ with uniformly converging boundary homeomorphisms satisfy
\[
 \delta_n\gamma(P_n)\Longrightarrow\mathrm{SLE}_3(D;a,b)
\]
at $\beta=\beta_c$. The topology is uniform distance modulo increasing reparametrization. Exterior completions may vary with the mesh subject to the stated parity and geometric conditions. The exterior completion is a finite subset $P_o\subset E\setminus E_\Omega$ of the full dual-edge set. The allowed set of interior contours with the prescribed odd-degree marks must be nonempty.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
An exact spin expansion translates contour energies into finite-range even interactions with the required pins. Buffered equilibrium comparisons and stopping-band resolution transfer the pure critical interface characterization to perturbed conditional laws, retaining full oriented-curve convergence.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The theorem gives the SLE interface limit at a domain-independent critical branch with the stated pure-model value. Its statement does not identify that branch through a magnetization or mass phase-transition definition for every signed contour perturbation. The target's additional physical-critical-coupling identification therefore remains a scope qualification.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 218, the formal scope is a finite-graph likelihood comparison through the zero-field FK connection probability after common pins are deleted. Stopping-band resolution and the universality companions are excluded. No Comparator is assigned to the selected manuscript here; the family page selects other papers or supporting statements. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

